   "score": 42,
   "text": "Hi Guys,\nlike many of you I work with AI agents every day and across several clients.\nThe major time cost for me is to re-explaining context and past decisions, client rules, that we already do. To finish every tools as its own memory.<p>So I\u2019m curious how you actually handle this:<p>1. When you start a new session, how do you give context to the agent (context came from chat, mail, ticket ...) ?<p>2. Do you use more than one agent type (claude, codex ...) ? And if yes, how do you carry context between agents ?<p>3. If you work for several clients, how do you keep their context separate ?<p>4. The last time something went wrong ( an agent used a rejected approach, forgot a decision ...), what happened, and how much time did it cost to you ?<p>5. Did you paid or built a tool that helped you with these problems ? Do you still use it ?<p>I\u2019m exploring whether to build something, so I\u2019m trying to learn how other people really work.\nThanks for your return.",
   "time": 1794045708,
   "title": "Ask HN: How do you manage your AI agents' context across clients and projects?",
   "type": "story",
   "_rank": 14
  },
  {
   "by": "rkaehn",
   "descendants": 5,
   "id": 50401844,
